8,Algonquian languages,https://www.azur.en-us.nina.az/Algonquian_languages.html,Algonquian. Algonkian. Geographic distribution. North America. Ethnicity. Algonquian peoples.Wiktionary has a list of reconstructed forms at Appendix:Proto-Algonquian reconstructions. The word 'woman' in the different Algonquian languages. Algic languages (from Proto-Algic).,Carolina Algonquian,Algic
9,Algic Language Family - Origins & Classification - MustGo,https://www.mustgo.com/worldlanguages/algic-language-family/,"The Algic language family is one of the largest indigenous language families of North America. It consists of 44 languages, the overwhelming majority of which (42 languages) belong to the Algonquian branch.",Carolina Algonquian,Algic
